  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohd Altaf Age 45 Years vs Union Territory Of Jammu And Kashmir on 2 April, 2024 Author: Sanjeev Kumar Bench: Sanjeev Kumar High Court Of Jammu & Kashmir And Ladakh At Jammu ... Hcp No. 68/2023 Reserved on: 07.03.2024 Pronounced on:02.04.2024 Mohd Altaf Age 45 years S/o Mohd. Iqbal Through his wife Khalida Kouser Age 40 years R/O Gadyog, Tehsil Khawas Rajouri. ......Petitioner(s) Through: Mr. Ayushman Kotwal, Advocate. Vs. 1. Union Territory of Jammu and Kashmir, Through Secretary Home Department, Civil Secretariat Jammu/ Srinagar. 2. District Magistrate Rajouri. 3. Sr. Superintendent of Police Rajouri. 4. Superintendent District Jail, Dhangiri, Rajouri. . .....Respondent(s) Through: Mr. Bhanu Jasrotia, Ga. Coram: Hon'Ble Mr Justice Sanjeev Kumar, Judge Judgement",
    "facts": "The respondent No.2 has, in the order of detention, referred to alleged commission of various offences and registration of FIR, but has not spelled out the involvement of the petitioner in the commission of any activity which has the potential of being prejudicial to the security of the State.",
    "arguments": "The respondent No.2 has thus failed to make a distinction between what is prejudicial to security of the State and what is only a problem of law and order; (ii) That the petitioner was not provided with the requisite material relied upon by the respondent No.2 to draw subjective satisfaction as a result whereof the petitioner was deprived of his right to make an effective representation to the Government against his detention; (iii) That the grounds of detention are vague and irrational and, therefore, vitiates the subjective satisfaction of the detaining authority. 5. Respondents have filed the counter affidavit of respondent No.2- District Magistrate. Mohd Altaf Age 45 Years vs Union Territory Of Jammu And Kashmir on 2 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/131894743/ 2 6."
  },
